Package: gkwqreg
Title: Parametric Quantile Regression for the Generalized Kumaraswamy Family
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "José Evandeilton", family = "Lopes",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "evandeilton@gmail.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-5887-4084"))
Description: Fixed-level parametric quantile regression for bounded responses in
    the open interval (0,1), using the five-parameter Generalized 'Kumaraswamy'
    distribution and its six nested sub-families. For a quantile level fixed in
    advance the distribution is reparametrized so that one parameter is the
    conditional quantile at that level, which is then modelled directly through a
    link function; the remaining parameters may carry their own regressions.
    Estimation is by maximum likelihood via 'TMB' automatic differentiation.
    Provides Wald, likelihood-ratio and sandwich inference, quantile-specific
    residuals and diagnostics, marginal effects, the quantile process over a grid
    of levels, and crossing detection. Generalizes the Kumaraswamy quantile
    reparametrization of Mitnik and Baek (2013) <doi:10.1007/s00362-011-0417-y>.
